---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import LandTrustWizard from '../../components/LandTrustWizard.tsx';

const title = 'Create Land Trust Agreement — Free Online Wizard';
const description = 'Generate a free Land Trust Agreement PDF in your browser. Answer a few questions, get a completed, signable document. No signup, nothing leaves your device.';

const legalServiceSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebApplication",
  "applicationCategory": "LegalApplication",
  "operatingSystem": "Web",
  "browserRequirements": "Requires JavaScript",
  "name": "FreeTrustDocs Land Trust Generator",
  "description": "Free online Land Trust Agreement generator. No signup required.",
  "url": "https://freetrustdocs.com/create/land-trust/",
  "publisher": {"@id": "https://freetrustdocs.com/#organization"},
  "areaServed": "US",
  "offers": {"@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "USD"}
};
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="breadcrumbs">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span>›</span>
        <a href="/land-trust/">Land Trust</a> <span>›</span> Create
      </div>

      <h1>Create Land Trust Agreement</h1>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        Answer the questions below. Your answers stay in your browser — no data is sent to any server.
        When you're done, you'll get a completed Land Trust Agreement PDF.
      </p>

      <LandTrustWizard client:load />

      <div class="sidebar-card">
        <strong>After creating your Land Trust Agreement:</strong>
        Keep your trust records organized with
        <a href="https://trustminutes.app?utm_source=freetrustdocs&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=funnel&utm_content=wizard_sidebar&utm_term=land_trust">
          TrustMinutes
        </a> (free). Then govern it with
        <a href="https://trustoffice.app?utm_source=freetrustdocs&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=funnel&utm_content=wizard_sidebar&utm_term=land_trust">
          TrustOffice
        </a>.

  <section class="section-tight" style="margin-top: 3rem;">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <h2>How a land trust works</h2>
      <p>A land trust holds legal title to real estate through a trustee, while you keep full control as the beneficiary. Because the recorded deed names only the trustee, your name stays off county property records. You keep the right to occupy the property, collect rent, sell, or refinance — all through a private direction that the trustee follows. Illinois and Florida are the best-known land-trust states, and several other states recognize the structure under common law.</p>

      <h2>What this generator produces</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A complete Land Trust Agreement naming the trustee, beneficiary, property, and term</li>
        <li>A Deed to Trustee for transferring the property into the trust</li>
        <li>A signature block with notary acknowledgment lines</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Both documents download as PDFs, ready to print and sign. The agreement is a private contract — only the deed gets recorded at the county level.</p>

      <h2>Why people use land trusts</h2>
      <p>Privacy is the most common reason: the public record shows the trustee, not you. Land trusts also let you assign beneficial interest without re-recording a deed, which simplifies transfers and estate planning. On properties with mortgages, the Garn-St. Germain Act generally shields transfers to inter vivos trusts where the borrower remains a beneficiary.</p>

      <h2>State-specific details</h2>
      <p>State pages cover the exact statutes, recording steps, and tax treatment:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/land-trust/illinois/">Illinois land trusts</a> — the original land-trust state, common-law based</li>
        <li><a href="/land-trust/florida/">Florida land trusts</a> — Florida Land Trust Act (§ 689.071)</li>
        <li><a href="/land-trust/virginia/">Virginia land trusts</a> — Va. Code § 55.1-117</li>
        <li><a href="/land-trust/ohio/">Ohio land trusts</a>, <a href="/land-trust/indiana/">Indiana</a>, <a href="/land-trust/north-dakota/">North Dakota</a>, and <a href="/land-trust/georgia/">Georgia</a></li>
        <li><a href="/land-trust/non-recognizing-states/">States without land-trust statutes</a> — including California and Texas</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Learn more</h2>
      <p>New to land trusts? Read the <a href="/guide/what-is-a-land-trust/">land trust overview</a> or compare a <a href="/guide/land-trust-vs-llc/">land trust vs. LLC</a>. For the full document walkthrough, see the <a href="/guide/land-trust-agreement/">Land Trust Agreement guide</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(legalServiceSchema)} />
</Base>